<title>FRANCE: Soros says euro delay could be &quot;catastrophe&quot;.</title>
<headline>Soros says euro delay could be &quot;catastrophe&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S.-based financier and investor George Soros said in an interview published on Thursday that a delay in implementation of European economic and monetary union could be a catastrophe.</p>
<p>&quot;I believe...that the single currency will happen, unless it is postponed, which could be a genuine catastrophe,&quot; Soros said in an interview with the French weekly L'Evenement du Jeudi.</p>
<p>The Hungarian-born investor and philanthropist, who heads the multibillion-dollar Quantum Group, added that he believed the single currency project had been &quot;poorly conceived&quot; and needed to be modified. He offered no details.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
